# scripts/opcount: `schemabench bench conforms N` checks one decoded value
# N times against its type's generated schema with jsonschema.Conforms
# (wf10 JS0); the cost of one check is the slope between the two sizes.
# The control is hand Go: the same value decoded by encoding/json into
# map[string]any, walked by a function written for that one schema. The
# floor is the typed value's own check: its union's tag compared to its
# variants' (a decoded record has every other property already).
unit check
sizes 100000 600000
args bench conforms {n}
control benchmarks/jsonschema/testdata/control
floor benchmarks/jsonschema/testdata/floor
